      "domain": "hpc_checkpointing",
      "title": "hpc checkpointing method",
      "summary": "An HPC job used Young's checkpoint interval approximation. With checkpoint time C and mean time between failures M, the variable overhead rate was C/T + T/(2M), minimized at T*=sqrt(2*C*M). A fixed restart time contributed R/M to overhead but did not change the minimizing T in this first-order model.",
